  "findings": [
    "Velocity RMS, fixed-interior pressure RMS, and rotor torque converge strongly while the unchanged global pressure maximum and eventually global pressure RMS do not converge.",
    "At level 8 the worst cell centre is 0.002715 m from a nonzero moving-wall trace jump. On the 96.74% fluid area at least 0.025 m from any such vertex, pressure RMS/maximum are 0.000590/0.01045 m2/s2 and decrease with refinement after the coarse level.",
    "The level-8 global pressure maximum is 0.6147 m2/s2 and remains in the evidence. This study does not grant pointwise pressure qualification at polygon vertices with a discontinuous prescribed tangential trace.",
    "The rigid-rotation product-operator patch remains at floating-point scale (level-8 maximum 3.61e-13 m/s2), excluding a general affine viscous inconsistency but not proving nonlinear or corner regularity.",
    "The combined evidence supports treating pointwise pressure at the fixed trace-discontinuity vertices as outside the qualified observable, while retaining full-field norms and explicit near-corner diagnostics. No solver, geometry, wall trace, threshold, or quality gate changed."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This is a polygon-versus-circular analytic comparison; it does not provide a closed-form polygon-corner pressure reference.",
    "The inference that the unresolved peak is tied to the fixed trace discontinuity follows from the fixed-geometry refinement and spatial localization; it is not a proof of a unique asymptotic exponent.",
    "Independent curved internal and external flows must still regress before any product-level applicability or output change. Entity-display desktop, macOS, and packaged applications are not tested here."
  ],
